60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option C is out. The cost of re-running power for a flexible layout is too high, and the billing is based on area.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I don't like Option C either. If I spend days making my chair feel right, I can't do that if I move every day.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Exactly! Option C is a nightmare. Imagine spending ten minutes every morning just to start working. No thank you.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is a coward's compromise. It just delays the inevitable frustration of sitting in a bad spot.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Um... Option A seems... safest? Because we know exactly who we are sitting next to... and we only pay the power fee once.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,@Daisuke is correct. Option A is the most fiscally responsible. We pay the installation fee once and we are done.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Minato,,"But if we use Option A, can we make sure the people who need quiet aren't by the door?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, we can just assign the seats that way! Option A is the only one that doesn't waste our time every morning.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, you're still thinking about ""comfort."" Let's talk about the window. Option A means we decide now who gets the light.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think Option A is better because we can actually decide... together... who sits where.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. Option A minimizes the risk of future costs and provides the stability the budget requires.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Minato,,"If we can agree to put the quietest people in the quietest spots, I'm okay with Option A.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,I'm all for Option A. I have too many meetings to spend my mornings playing musical chairs.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,Fine. Option A it is. At least we can have a proper argument about who gets the window before we sign the check.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we're agreeing. I think Option A is the best way to make sure we're okay with our neighbors.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
